From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:33:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: tasks card gets an always-visible scrollbar,
 dismiss and Clear finished
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wave 2 of the Zeo next proposal (docs/ZEO-NEXT-PROPOSAL.md §5.2, asks 4,
32, 33; finding F2). Patch 0037's card capped its list at 24 rem and
scrolled it, but drew no scrollbar, no row could be dismissed and there
was no clear-all: an ended row left only when its 10 s linger ran out,
and a native subagent row in state Unknown stayed while its parent was
held.

- The list keeps its 24 rem cap and now draws its scrollbar always, the
  way the Agent Tasks panel does (`Scrollbars::always_visible`, tracked
  by a `ScrollHandle` the card holds): `Scrollbars::new` hides the thumb
  a second after the pointer enters, which story 034 measured.
- An "×" on every row in a terminal state and on rows in state Unknown;
  running and waiting rows keep Stop. An ended row leaves at once (its
  linger entry is dropped); an Unknown row is hidden while it stays
  Unknown and comes back if it turns Running.
- "Clear finished" in the header, shown while any such row is on show,
  does both for every row.

Dismissing is the card's alone: the Agent Tasks panel, its history and
the tray keep every record. Sub-thread rows (story 040) are not
dismissable yet.

Tests: tasks_card/dismiss_tests.rs — an ended row dismissed leaves and
the card hides; a running row cannot be dismissed; Clear finished keeps
the running row. The scrollbar and the Unknown-row dismissal are not
covered by a test (Xvfb, and the native-subagent fixture). Verified 2026-11-09 in the prepared d2a4fb6 tree: cargo check --tests, cargo clippy --tests and cargo fmt --check clean, cargo test passing, on acp_thread, agent_servers, agent_ui and sidebar.

Fixed in Zeo 0.9.1 (operator report, 2026-11-09): with every row dismissed,
or nothing left running, the card stayed on screen, and minimized it showed a
spinning "0". Two causes. rows() ordered a group by its live rows before the
dismissal filter ran, so a group whose last live row was a dismissed Unknown
child kept a running order with no rows, and an empty group kept the card
visible; the order is now read after the filter, and a group with nothing
left leaves. The pill always drew the spinner and the running count, which
also left out running sub-threads; it now spins only while something runs,
and otherwise counts what the card holds under a still ListTodo icon ("1
task, none running"). Unknown rows still hold the card: a child that has not
reported yet reads Unknown, and story 064's R1.1 shows it on spawn.

Tests (native_subagent_tests.rs), each seen failing first:
test_dismissing_the_last_unknown_row_hides_the_card and
test_the_pill_does_not_spin_or_count_zero_while_nothing_runs; with the guard
test_the_pill_spins_while_a_child_runs, which passed before and after.
